#!/bin/sh
# {{ ansible_managed }}
# Plasma: sets the netstation wallpaper on every screen, once per home
# folder. The automatic login gets a fresh home every time, so it always gets
# it; users with their own account keep the wallpaper they pick themselves.
# plasmashell may still be starting, so it tries for up to a minute.
wallpaper=/usr/share/backgrounds/netstation/{{ netstation_wallpaper_file | quote }}
done_file=${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/netstation-wallpaper-set
[ -e "$done_file" ] && exit 0
for _ in $(seq 30); do
    if plasma-apply-wallpaperimage "$wallpaper" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
        mkdir -p "$(dirname "$done_file")" && touch "$done_file"
        exit 0
    fi
    sleep 2
done
logger -t netstation-wallpaper -- "plasma-apply-wallpaperimage $wallpaper failed"
